    {
      "name": "Basic Attack Build",
      "label": "Situational",
      "description": "The Basic Attack Build takes Talents that dramatically improve Hanzo's sustained damage. As with any ranged Basic Attack strategy, you want to position yourself near maximum range while delivering Basic Attacks to enemy Heroes.\n\nNever Outmatched significantly reduces the cooldown of Scatter Arrow and enhances your overall damage output. However, new Hanzo players might find it challenging to get used to, as the increased attack speed from Redemption requires quick use of Scatter Arrow after every two Basic Attacks. Sharpened Arrowheads is an easier yet still excellent option, as each consecutive Basic Attack or Storm Bow hit on an enemy Hero reduces their armor for 3 seconds, increasing all damage done to that enemy.\n\nGiant Slayer works very well against enemy Tanks with large health pools. If the enemy frontline is lacking and you need finishing power against squishy enemy Heroes, Flawless Technique can be a good choice instead.",
